sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant E as Editor
    participant L as Browser replica
    participant IDB as Account-scoped outbox
    participant S as Instance 1
    participant DB as Postgres log
    participant R as Redis
    participant O as Instance 2

    E->>L: keystroke
    L->>L: insert and assign operation id
    L-->>E: paint without a server round trip
    L->>IDB: persist operation
    IDB-->>L: transaction committed
    L->>S: SEND operation
    S->>S: validate session, access and actor ownership
    S->>S: merge and broadcast to local clients
    S->>DB: append batch with stable identity claim
    DB-->>S: commit and server sequence
    S-->>L: durable acknowledgment
    L->>IDB: forget acknowledged operation
    S->>R: publish committed operations, best effort
    R->>O: merge and deliver to other clients
    Note over S,O: anti-entropy replays Postgres to repair missed delivery
    Note over L,S: a fast broadcast never releases the outbox
